From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:36:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] null renderer: primitive restart, the provoking vertex,
 polygon offset, the alpha test and point coordinates in software draws

Indexed draws with primitive restart are drawn as the runs of indices between restart
indices. Flat varyings come from the first vertex or the last, as the provoking vertex
register says. Polygon offset (for triangles, lines and points, each as enabled) adds the
depth bias: the constant in the depth format's smallest step (the register's half, as
Eden's Vulkan renderer takes it) and the slope factor times the depth's steepest slope,
clamped. The alpha test discards what fails against render target 0's alpha. A fragment
shader's point coordinates (gl_PointCoord) run from 0 to 1 across each point, t down from
the top as Eden's Vulkan renderer has it.
---
 .../renderer_null/software_draw.cpp           | 112 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 93 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_null/software_draw.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_null/software_draw.cpp
